---
layout: base.njk
title: Pledges
description: Promises made in Malta's manifestos, budgets and announcements, labelled by whether they can be measured and how they are progressing, with an as-of date, who made them, when, and which pledges overlap.
permalink: /pledges/
---
{%- import "macros.njk" as m -%}
{%- set P = mizien.pledges -%}
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Pledges</li></ol>
</nav>

<article class="page prose-page pledges-page">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Pledges</p>
    <h1>Pledges</h1>
    <p class="lead">A pledge is a promise of future action, so it gets a label instead of a verdict: whether it can be
      measured and, if so, how it is going. Every label carries an <em>as of</em> date, the date of the evidence behind it.</p>
  </header>

  <p class="see-also">{% icon "links" %}<a href="/explore/?group=pledges">See the pledges election by election in Explore</a>: one disk
    per election cycle, campaign pledges on the outer ring and commitments made in office on the inner ring, with lines from a
    pledge to the earlier one it carries forward (red where the earlier one was not met) and between pledges that overlap.</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-labels">
    <h2 id="h-labels">The labels</h2>
    <dl class="pledge-labels">
      {%- for l in mizien.pledge_labels %}
      <div><dt><span class="badge {{ l.slug }} v-{{ l.slug }}">{{ l.name }}</span></dt><dd>{{ l.meaning | mdInline | safe }}</dd></div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
    <p class="small">A check of a pledge alone shows only its label. A check that also tests factual statements keeps its
      verdict for those and shows the label beside it. Decided on 5 October 2026; see the Pledges section of
      <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/methodology/verdict-scale.md#pledges">the verdict scale</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-list">
    <h2 id="h-list">Pledges checked so far</h2>
    {%- if P.length %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="claims pledge-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Pledge</th><th scope="col">Made by</th><th scope="col">Made in</th><th scope="col">Deadline</th><th scope="col">Label</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {%- for x in P %}
        <tr><td>{{ m.claim(x) }}<br><span class="small">{{ x.pledge.target }}</span></td>
          <td>{% for b in x.pledge.made_by %}<a href="{{ b.path }}">{{ b.name }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
          <td>{{ x.pledge.vehicle }}{% if x.pledge.made_on %}<br><span class="small">{{ x.pledge.made_on }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{{ x.pledge.deadline or "none stated" }}{% if x.pledge.term_end %}<br><span class="small">term ended {{ x.pledge.term_end }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
          <td><span class="badge v-{{ x.pledge.slug }}">{{ x.pledge.status }}</span><br><span class="small">as of {{ x.pledge.as_of }}</span>
            {%- if x.verdict %}<br><span class="small">verdict on the facts: {{ x.verdict }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
      {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    {%- else %}
    <p>No pledge is labelled yet.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  {%- set OL = mizien.outlier_list %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-outliers">
    <h2 id="h-outliers">Outliers</h2>
    <p>The usual chain runs from a campaign promise to a commitment in office to an outcome. An outlier breaks that chain.
      Each is stated as a finding with the record it rests on, never inferred from a gap, and never about motive. The
      rules are in the Outliers part of <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/methodology/verdict-scale.md#pledges">the verdict scale</a>.</p>
    {%- set types = [
      ["recycled", "Recycled", "The same promise made again in a later election while the earlier one was not met. Applies to every party."],
      ["drift", "Drift", "A commitment linked to an earlier promise, but changed from it: a target lowered, a deadline moved, the scope narrowed or the measure changed."],
      ["unanchored", "Unanchored", "A government commitment with no earlier pledge behind it. Shown only after a recorded search of the manifestos."],
      ["dropped", "Dropped", "A campaign pledge of the governing party with no follow-up in office. Shown only after the legislature has ended and a search is recorded."]
    ] %}
    {%- for t in types %}
    {%- set items = OL | where("type", t[0]) %}
    <h3 id="outlier-{{ t[0] }}">{{ t[1] }} <span class="small">({{ items.length }})</span></h3>
    <p class="small">{{ t[2] }}</p>
    {%- if items.length %}
    <ul class="outliers">
      {%- for o in items %}
      <li>{% if o.claim %}{{ m.claim(o.claim) }}{% else %}<a href="/pledges/manifestos/#{{ o.manifesto.id }}">{{ o.manifesto.name }}</a>
        <span class="small">({{ o.manifesto.summary | replace(r/\.$/, "") }}; in the manifesto list, not checked)</span>{% endif %}
        <br>{{ o.text | mdInline | safe }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- elif t[0] == "dropped" %}
    <p class="none">None recorded yet. The 2022–26 legislature has ended; the check of the governing party's 2022
      pledges for a follow-up in office has not been done.</p>
    {%- elif t[0] == "unanchored" %}
    <p class="none">None recorded yet. A commitment is listed here only after a recorded search finds no earlier pledge.</p>
    {%- else %}
    <p class="none">None recorded yet.</p>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- set fw = OL | where("type", "follows") %}
    {%- if fw.length %}
    <h3 id="carried-forward">Carried forward <span class="small">({{ fw.length }})</span></h3>
    <p class="small">Not outliers: a commitment that takes forward an earlier pledge, as recorded. Shown so that the chains
      can be followed, and on <a href="/explore/?group=pledges">the cycle disks in Explore</a>.</p>
    <ul class="outliers">
      {%- for o in fw %}
      <li>{% if o.claim %}{{ m.claim(o.claim) }}{% else %}<a href="/pledges/manifestos/#{{ o.manifesto.id }}">{{ o.manifesto.name }}</a>{% endif %}
        <br>{{ o.text | mdInline | safe }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  {%- set MC = mizien.manifesto_coverage %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-manifestos">
    <h2 id="h-manifestos">The manifesto list</h2>
    <p>So that pledges can be linked across elections, Miżien keeps a light list of the pledges in each programme: the
      whole of every environment chapter and every climate and energy chapter, for every party that contested the
      election, to the same scope. Each is a summary in our own words with its number and page. Most have not been
      checked; a listed pledge carries no label until it is.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="claims mp-coverage">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Election</th><th scope="col">Party</th><th scope="col">Programme</th><th scope="col">Pledges listed</th><th scope="col">With a target</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {%- for c in MC %}
        <tr><td>{{ c.cycle }}</td><td>{{ c.party_name }}</td>
          <td>{% if c.status == "listed" %}<a href="/pledges/manifestos/#{{ c.anchor }}">{{ c.document }}</a>{% else %}<span class="small">{{ c.status | capitalize }}. {{ c.searched }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{{ c.rows if c.status == "listed" else "–" }}</td><td>{{ c.measurable if c.status == "listed" else "–" }}</td></tr>
      {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Counts differ because programmes differ in length and layout, not in scope. "With a target": the
      pledge states a quantity, date or deadline that could be checked. <a href="/pledges/manifestos/">Browse the list</a>.</p>
  </section>

  {%- set overlapping = P | having("overlaps.length") %}
  {%- if overlapping.length %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-overlaps">
    <h2 id="h-overlaps">Overlapping pledges</h2>
    <p>Pledges overlap when they are listed as overlapping, share a theme, or are on the same subtopic. Overlapping
      pledges are worth reading together, for example when two parties promise to tackle the same problem.</p>
    <ul class="linked-bodies">
      {%- for x in overlapping %}
      <li><p class="lb-name">{{ m.claim(x) }}</p>
        {%- for o in x.overlaps %}<p class="lb-why">Overlaps {{ m.claim(o) }}: {{ o.why | join("; ") }}.</p>{% endfor %}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}
</article>
